{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-ba2fde1f5efbaf1b9b5e2a08b8ec8c24880a3e9f29ece160","family_id":"KR:006574","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Enforcement Rules of the Traffic, Energy and Environment Tax Act","title_original":"교통ㆍ에너지ㆍ환경세법 시행규칙","kind":"기획재정부령","source_version":"270243","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=270243","source_sha256":"99129fa87198dde7d65113cb7db1fbce6f402e0eebdd4849d79cfbe3f5e1d12e","body_sha256":"6a7e84bf041fb68a28c6b5644f302cd423025e0ff74547c238307ff34ca3698b","article_count":0,"full_text":"[Partial Amendment]\n\n◇ Reasons for Amendment and Main Contents\n\nThe Enforcement Decree of the Traffic, Energy and Environment Tax Act was amended (Presidential Decree No. 35356, promulgated on February 28, 2025, and effective on April 1, 2025) to prevent the unlawful distribution of tax-exempt petroleum products used by foreign-going vessels or deep-sea fishing vessels. The amendment requires the statement of fuel supply submitted when reporting the entry of such articles to the head of the competent tax office or customs office to include materials proving that the fuel was supplied for tax-exempt purposes, among other materials. Accordingly, these Rules are intended to require submission of data on fuel quantities measured using a mass flow meter where a mass flow meter is installed on the bunkering vessel, and, where no mass flow meter is installed on the bunkering vessel, documents that can verify the sealing of the bunkering vessel's fuel tanks and the supply of fuel in the specified quantity.\n\n<Provided by the Ministry of Economy and Finance>\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_source_review_evidence":[{"evidence":{